Option: qr-stronger
Name: QR signs: stronger codes (error correction Q)
Does: tools/make_qr.py makes the codes at error correction level Q (a sign that is wet, torn or faded still scans if about 25 percent of it is damaged, not about 15) instead of M. Each code has a few more squares (for example the directions code 49 to 57 across), so each square prints 10 to 15 percent smaller; the print-qr test still passes (smallest square above the 1.06 mm it asks for). The patch carries the codes and sign pages made by tools/make_qr.py: the 8 files in assets/qr/ that change (instagram.svg stays: the tool already raised it to Q) and print/qr-signs.html with the hi, zh and vi sheets. Print one sign and scan it with a phone before the signs go up.
Answers: d65 B (stronger codes; with qr-one-line it is d65 D, both)
Conflicts: none
Requires: none
Host: any
Order: 72
Profile: filled
After: nothing is needed (the codes and sign pages are in the patch); after a later change to tools/qr_links.json or reviewUrl run python3 tools/make_qr.py. If an assets/ or print/ hunk does not fit because a sign changed, apply with git apply --exclude='assets/*' --exclude='print/*' and run python3 tools/make_qr.py
Strings: none

